From: Uke Linux project <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libssc: make Python mock tests optional

Upstream: libssc 0.4.4, archive SHA256
716d6bd6b34d2d753060c6b54c9a87e34fae75b724c763bf9ef487efa3621587

Keep upstream test behavior by default. Native runtime builds can disable
the mock/test subtree so no Python server is installed on the tablet.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -101,7 +101,11 @@
 headers = files()
 map_source = files('libssc.map')
 
-subdir('mocking')
+if get_option('tests')
+  subdir('mocking')
+endif
 subdir('data')
 subdir('src')
-subdir('tests')
+if get_option('tests')
+  subdir('tests')
+endif
--- /dev/null
+++ b/meson.options
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+option('tests', type: 'boolean', value: true, description: 'Build SSC tests and Python mock server')
